The security team follows the changes in the regulations and standards that apply to the organisation. It updates the compliance register, the internal controls, the process descriptions, and the templates when needed.

== How to decide if this control is required

This control is required when the organisation is in the scope of security regulation, for example NIS2, the CRA, or the GDPR, or when its customers require compliance with standards.

== How to implement

. Name the sources to follow. For example: the regulation of the EU and of the other countries where the organisation operates or sells its products, the guidance of the authorities, and the standards that the customers require.
. Name the person who follows each source. Use the central security role assignments of this home.
. Review the changes at least once a year. Record the changes that affect the organisation, and the actions.
. Update the compliance register, the internal controls, the process descriptions, and the templates. Create a task for each larger change.

{{#report}}
  "name": "ismsa/reports/createEvidence",
